course: dictionary
lesson: 11635
title: Arithmetic
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Arithmetic is the part of maths about numbers. It uses the four basic operations: adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing. When you work out 7 + 5 or 6 × 4, you are doing arithmetic.
explain: «Mia did the arithmetic in her head before the bus arrived.» Here arithmetic means working out sums with numbers. Check your meaning by asking: does it involve numbers and the four operations? If yes, it is arithmetic.
explain: Arithmetic is an uncountable noun, so we say «good arithmetic», not «an arithmetic». The adjective arithmetical describes things linked to it, as in «an arithmetical puzzle». Mental arithmetic means working out sums in your head.
fact: Arithmetic is the part of maths about numbers and the four basic operations.
fact: The four basic operations are adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing.
fact: «Arithmetic» can also mean how good someone is at working out sums.
fact: An arithmetic sequence adds the same number each time, such as 2, 5, 8, 11.
fact: We use arithmetic when shopping, cooking or telling the time.
exercise: «Mia did the arithmetic in her head before the bus arrived.» What does arithmetic mean here? | Reading stories aloud | Drawing pictures of buses | *Working out sums with numbers | Walking very quickly
exercise: Which of these is an example of arithmetic? | *Adding 45 and 27 | Painting a picture of a tree | Singing a song | Reading a story about dragons
exercise: The arithmetic sequence 2, 5, 8, 11 goes on. What is the next number? | 16 | 13 | *14 | 19
test: «The shop assistant did the arithmetic quickly and gave me the right change.» What is arithmetic in this sentence? | *Working out sums with numbers | Writing a shop sign | Wrapping parcels in paper | Talking politely to customers
test: Which word is the adjective? | Sum | Arithmetic | *Arithmetical | Number
exam: What is the best meaning of arithmetic? | Measuring the length of a room | Drawing shapes and patterns | *The part of maths about numbers and adding, subtracting, multiplying and dividing | Reading maps and plans
